From d0c7335c579e171245df2cb95ba725e3e1b1da9c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kevin Pratap Sidhu <pratapkevin8@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 12:38:35 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] [NUI] Add pipe backend: live depth from a local named
 pipe

--nui=pipe --nui_pipe=<name> serves \\.\pipe\<name> and publishes the
depth frames another local process writes into it, as a live .xdepth
stream (DepthRecordingHeader, then frames). It lets a host-side depth
source that is not a Kinect, such as a webcam pipeline that synthesises
depth, drive a title without being built into xenia.

Inbound only, one client, remote clients rejected. Overlapped I/O, so
Shutdown() returns while a read is pending. When the writer goes away
the last frame stays current and the pipe is offered again. Tilt
follows the replay backend's requested-angle model. Windows only;
"any" picks it only when nui_pipe names a pipe.

Tested: xenia-nui-tests pass (81 cases, 37142 assertions); Kinect
Adventures (4D5308ED) reached its title screen with a PLAYING player on
5100 recorded frames streamed through the pipe, and logged the writer
leaving and the wait for the next one.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
